#Tetris

A simple clone of the classic game **Tetris**, built with Python using the **Pygame** library.
The core game logic was inspired by [this implementation](https://gist.github.com/timurbakibayev/1f683d34487362b0f36280989c80960c).
This project was developed for educational purposes to practice game development and Python programming skills.
The game features a scoring system and persistent high-score tracking.

##Screenshots
![Main Menu](pictures/1.png)
![Gameplay](pictures/2.png)

##Project Structure
The project is organized into several modules for better readability and maintenance:
```text
Tetris/
│
├── main.py            # Main game loop and entry point
├── music_player.py    # Class for handling background music
├── settings.py        # Game configurations and constants
├── tetris.py          # Core game logic and mechanics
├── drawning.py        # Functions for rendering game elements (UI/Graphics)
├── figure.py          # Class representing Tetris blocks (tetrominos)
├── resources/
│   ├── highscore.json # Stores the all-time high score
│   ├── background/    # Directory for background images
│   └── music/         # Directory for audio files
└── README.md

Autor: kamikaj
